WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.390
- You have done "SNL",
Broadway, so many things,

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.520
but is it true that your
greatest achievement

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.440
is bargain hunting?

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.300
One of my friends is great at this.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.320
Are you really great at this?

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.153
I'm not good at this.

00:00:11.153 --> 00:00:12.330
- You're not?
- No.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.397
And I grew up with no money, I just...

00:00:13.397 --> 00:00:14.640
- What about your Wayfair plug?

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.768
- Well, here's my thing. No.

00:00:15.768 --> 00:00:17.743
(audience laughs)

00:00:17.743 --> 00:00:19.290
I'm not good at bargaining,
like in this sense

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.009
of like going out and getting something.

00:00:21.009 --> 00:00:21.842
- Okay.

00:00:21.842 --> 00:00:23.959
- I'm good at getting you
bargains, you're welcome.

00:00:23.959 --> 00:00:26.700
- But I'm not good at like going out

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.960
or like if you go to like a flea market

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.240
and people are like, oh
you can like talk 'em down,

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.410
like I'm, mm.
- I'm not good at that either

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.670
'cause I get shy and embarrassed

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.470
and I don't want people
to think I'm cheap.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.490
- Yeah, yeah. I guess, yeah.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.170
- So I panic on that for sure.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.850
Like, I'll pick up the
whole bill at dinner

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.121
instead of like argue over
how many Cokes somebody had.

00:00:41.121 --> 00:00:41.954
- [Kelly] 100%.

00:00:41.954 --> 00:00:42.840
- Okay, that's fine.
- Yes.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.400
- But I get a lot of like,
dopamine hits from being thrifty.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.580
Like, so, if I find something cheap.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.650
Or if I find, like I paid
for all of our flights

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.170
to Europe using points and miles.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.630
So, and it was like the
scene from "Homeland"

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.550
or like "A Beautiful Mind",
like I was like swapping,

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.640
like I can move the Hilton
over to American points.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.487
And my husband's like,

00:01:03.487 --> 00:01:05.310
"Literally you could
be doing anything else

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.210
and making money right now."

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.560
But anyway, but I get really,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.431
like the thrill of it's amazing.

00:01:09.431 --> 00:01:10.264
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:10.264 --> 00:01:11.370
- And the thrill of the hunt is great.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.710
Like finding something and getting a steal

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.570
and that makes me really excited.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.910
- Okay, so I get this,
my sister once told me,

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:18.990
I had no idea, right.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.480
So I was like an Amazon
Prime member or whatever.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.780
And I don't work for them,
so this isn't like a plug.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.120
I just mean I didn't
know and I was, you know,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.950
paying for birthday parties
and paying for things,

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.360
like things that you get for things,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.280
just constantly, right?
- Yes, yes.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.710
- And 'cause I'm a working
mom, single, whatever.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:38.160
My sister was like, Hey, by
the way, did you realize.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.450
I had, this is not a joke, like six mil,

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.760
it was like some crazy 6 million points

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.680
or something because I used my-

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:47.670
- Amex
- Some...Amex?

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:48.503
Yeah, card or something.

00:01:48.503 --> 00:01:49.650
And I was like, "What do you mean?"

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:54.630
So then I proceeded to shop
for like two years for free.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:55.560
- That's incredible.
- On Amazon.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.687
And I was like, "What?"

00:01:57.859 --> 00:01:59.180
(audience claps and cheers)

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.390
And every time I'd say, use
my points and it goes zero,

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.280
it doesn't matter how much
money you have in life,

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.239
it feels good.

00:02:06.239 --> 00:02:07.072
- Oh, it feels great.

00:02:07.072 --> 00:02:07.950
So here's the best one I ever did.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.800
Okay, so we have a house on Fire Island,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.660
which is like a little beach community.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.370
- [Kelly] I've heard of Fire Island, yeah.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.980
- It's a barrier reef island
off the coast of Long Island.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.080
Anyway, a lot of rich people
throw away their stuff

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.400
at the beginning of the season,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.410
which makes for really
great bargain hunting,

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.550
'cause they'll clean out the house

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.870
'cause they're preparing
to rent their house

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.974
or whatever, so it's-

00:02:25.974 --> 00:02:26.897
- What about those garage sales?

00:02:26.897 --> 00:02:28.560
- That's I'm saying, they
don't have a garage sale.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.180
They just put it on their, like,

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.640
those like little trash,
you know, box things

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.350
to keep the deer from eating your trash.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.183
Do you know what I'm talking about?

00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:36.570
- Yeah, yeah, that you
keep for bears or whatever.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.740
- Yes, exactly.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:38.820
So they put their stuff out.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.530
So one time I, one
weekend I was walking by

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.140
and there was a perfectly
good Nespresso machine.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.060
I already had a Nespresso machine

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.770
which I had gotten for my birthday,

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.603
but a month later

00:02:47.603 --> 00:02:49.710
there was a perfectly
good Nespresso machine.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:50.543
It looked brand new.

00:02:50.543 --> 00:02:52.290
I took it home, I was super excited.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.190
I poured water through it.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.380
It poured straight out the
bottom and all over my floor.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.310
Okay.
- Oh.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.165
- Under-
- You see why it was-

00:02:57.165 --> 00:02:58.833
- Got it.
- Got it, yeah.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:00.923
But you know what I did?

00:03:00.923 --> 00:03:02.250
I was like, "This thing looks new."

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.500
So I picked up the phone
and I called Nespresso

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.170
and they're like, "Oh yeah,
that serial number is new.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.430
I'll send you a new one."

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:09.660
Completely new.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.075
So I gave it to my friend
Sally for her 40th birthday.

00:03:12.075 --> 00:03:13.423
- Look at that.

00:03:13.423 --> 00:03:14.256
- Because, yes.

00:03:14.256 --> 00:03:15.089
(audience claps)

00:03:15.089 --> 00:03:17.610
And the greatest thing
is she's also thrifty.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:18.870
So I told her the whole story.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.840
She was like so extra excited
that it was trash picked.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.850
- Yes, that's thoughtful.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.871
- She trash picked a solar
once in Brooklyn, so yeah.

00:03:26.871 --> 00:03:27.900
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:28.770
- Friendship.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:29.603
- Yeah.

